---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'How sameetsapra.com is built and run: Astro on GitHub Pages, a warm-paper design in Fraunces and Inter, generated data pages, and an AI agent that does the publishing.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Colophon" description={description}>
  <div class="measure">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>How this site is made — and who makes it.</p>

      <h2>Stack</h2>
      <p>
        The site is built with <strong>Astro</strong> and hosted on
        <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. Content is plain markdown.
        There is no database, no analytics, and no tracking. Pages
        are static HTML; the only JavaScript on the site powers the
        <a href="/places/">Places</a> map's city cards.
      </p>

      <h2>Design</h2>
      <p>
        A warm-paper palette — paper <code>#f7f0e1</code>, ink
        <code>#211a12</code>, terracotta <code>#9c3d20</code> — set in
        <strong>Fraunces</strong> for display type and
        <strong>Inter</strong> for text, both self-hosted. Post pages
        get a reading treatment: serif body text, a byline with a
        computed reading time, and an author card. Every post also
        generates its own share card (title, summary, date) at build
        time.
      </p>

      <h2>The data pages</h2>
      <p>
        Places is generated, not hand-written: a script builds it
        from my own Google Maps reviews and Beli rankings. The world
        map is a static SVG drawn from Natural Earth data — no map
        tiles, no API keys.
      </p>

      <h2>Run by an agent</h2>
      <p>
        This site is managed by <strong>Muse</strong>, an AI agent,
        under my direction — that's what the footer on every page
        means. The workflow is the same for every change: I say what
        I want, the agent builds it locally and shows me previews, I
        approve or correct, and only then does it publish — there's a
        running log of those changes in the site's history. Research,
        drafting, code, data pipelines, publishing: delegated.
        Taste, judgment, and the final word: not delegated.
      </p>

      <h2>Standards</h2>
      <p>
        An <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>, a sitemap, structured
        data on every page, and an
        <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> for AI tools that want the
        short version.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
